1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,420
Ask most people which day of the week they dread the most and the answer is likely to be Monday.
问大多数人一周中最害怕哪一天，答案很可能是周一。

2
00:00:07,420 --> 00:00:15,620
The first day of the week can make us grouchy and depressed, which is why the feeling is described as the Monday blues.
一周的第一天总会让我们变得烦躁又低落，这种情绪也因此被称为“周一忧郁症”。

3
00:00:15,620 --> 00:00:21,980
But what is it exactly that makes us feel down and does it affect everyone?
但究竟是什么让我们心情变差，这种情绪又会影响每一个人吗？

4
00:00:21,980 --> 00:00:31,020
Apparently, the most depressing day of the year is the third Monday in January, when it’s cold and dark outside.
显然，一年中最让人沮丧的日子是一月的第三个周一，彼时室外天寒地冻、昼短夜长。

5
00:00:31,020 --> 00:00:38,290
This day was nicknamed ‘Blue Monday’ by psychologist Cliff Arnall in 2004.
心理学家克利夫·阿诺尔在2004年将这一天命名为“蓝色星期一”。

6
00:00:38,290 --> 00:00:46,420
He came up with it after a holiday company asked him for a ‘scientific formula’ for the January blues.
当时一家度假公司请他推算出一个解释“一月忧郁症”的“科学公式”，这个说法便由此诞生。

7
00:00:46,420 --> 00:01:01,410
Even if there was little science behind the formula, it’s probably true that the sound of our alarm clock on any Monday morning signals the dawning of a new week and possibly the end of our weekend of fun.
尽管这个公式并没有太多科学依据，但有一点或许是事实：每个周一清晨的闹钟声，都意味着新一周的开始，也可能宣告着充满乐趣的周末就此结束。

8
00:01:01,410 --> 00:01:07,920
Research shows our Monday mood can be based on a direct comparison to the day before.
研究表明，我们周一的心情好坏，往往源于与前一天的直接对比。

9
00:01:07,920 --> 00:01:16,010
It’s what psychologists call an emotional shift, and no other part of the week has a transition like it.
这就是心理学家所说的“情绪转变”，一周之中再也没有哪个时段会有如此强烈的状态切换。

10
00:01:16,010 --> 00:01:34,060
Monday means the end of weekend lie-ins – it’s back to the routine and the realisation that there are five days ahead of the nine-to-five, and according to the BBC Bitesize website “If you can’t stand your job then the Monday blues can be very real.”
周一意味着周末懒觉的终结——大家要重新回归日常工作生活，同时意识到朝九晚五的日子还要持续五天。英国广播公司教学科普网站BBC Bitesize提到：“如果你无法忍受自己的工作，那么周一忧郁症就会真实地找上门来。”

11
00:01:34,060 --> 00:01:42,570
And your miserable Monday is followed by trying Tuesday – the most popular day for sending out job applications.
在令人郁闷的周一过后，接踵而至的是“求职周二”——这一天是人们投递求职信的高峰期。

12
00:01:42,570 --> 00:01:47,140
But is Monday as bad as we like to think it is?
但周一真的像我们想象中那么糟糕吗？

13
00:01:47,140 --> 00:01:54,380
Feeling a bit low shouldn’t be confused with more serious depression, caused by other factors.
这种轻微的低落情绪，不应与由其他因素引发的更为严重的抑郁症混为一谈。

14
00:01:54,380 --> 00:02:02,730
Writing for the BBC, author and presenter Claudia Hammond, argues that this low feeling might be a myth.
作家兼主持人克劳迪娅·哈蒙德在为BBC撰写的文章中指出，这种对周一的抵触感可能只是一种错误的固有印象。

15
00:02:02,730 --> 00:02:08,720
She says: “There is a strong cultural idea that we don’t like Mondays.”
她表示：“不喜欢周一已经成了一种根深蒂固的文化观念。”

16
00:02:08,720 --> 00:02:21,640
She mentions an Australian study in 2008 about how people reflected on their mood and found the day that scored the lowest was in fact Wednesdays.
她还提到2008年澳大利亚的一项研究，该研究调查了人们对自身情绪的回顾，结果发现情绪最低落的日子其实是周三。

17
00:02:21,640 --> 00:02:27,760
So, when Monday comes, maybe we should give it a second chance!
所以，当周一来临时，或许我们应该再给它一次机会！
